## 1.2 Google Hacking (Google Dorking)

Google Hacking is the technique of using advanced Google search operators to discover publicly indexed information.

It can help identify exposed files, public documents, login pages, and information related to a target.

### Common Google Search Operators

|Operator|Purpose|
|---|---|
|`site:`|Restricts results to a specific domain or website.|
|`filetype:`|Searches for files with a specific extension.|
|`-filetype:`|Excludes files with a specific extension.|
|`intitle:`|Searches for a specific word in the page title.|
|`inurl:`|Searches for a specific word in the URL.|
|`intext:`|Searches for a specific word in the page content.|

### Examples

**1. Search within a specific domain**

```
site:example.com
```

Returns indexed pages associated with `example.com`.

**2. Search for PDF files**

```
site:example.com filetype:pdf
```

Finds indexed PDF files on the target domain.

**3. Exclude PDF files**

```
site:example.com -filetype:pdf
```

Excludes PDF files from the search results.

**4. Search for pages with a specific title**

```
site:example.com intitle:login
```

Searches for pages on the domain containing `login` in their titles.

### Google Hacking Database (GHDB)

The **Google Hacking Database (GHDB)** is a collection of Google Dorks that can help security professionals discover publicly exposed information.

It is maintained by Exploit Database.

**Reference:**  
[https://www.exploit-db.com/google-hacking-database](https://www.exploit-db.com/google-hacking-database)

### DorkSearch

DorkSearch is a tool that helps construct Google Dorks using search operators.

**Reference:**  
[https://dorksearch.com/](https://dorksearch.com/)

