## 1.4 Open-Source Code

Public source-code repositories can contain useful information about an organization's infrastructure, applications, and technologies.

During reconnaissance, we can search for publicly available repositories associated with the target.

### Common Platforms

- **GitHub:** [https://github.com/](https://github.com/)
    
- **GitLab:** [https://gitlab.com/](https://gitlab.com/)
    
- **SourceForge:** [https://sourceforge.net/](https://sourceforge.net/)
    

### What to look for

- Organization-owned repositories.
    
- Application source code.
    
- Configuration files.
    
- API endpoints.
    
- Internal hostnames accidentally included in code.
    
- Development and deployment documentation.
    
- Exposed credentials or secrets.
    

**Important:** Finding credentials or secrets in public repositories does not authorize their use. Treat them as sensitive information and report them through the appropriate responsible disclosure channel.

